### http_core — default limits are the shared contract

#### publishes the same default limits both transports enforce

- Read the shared limit constants
   - Expected: MAX_REQUEST_LINE equals `8192)  # oracle: 8192 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: MAX_HEADER_COUNT equals `100)  # oracle: 100 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: MAX_HEADER_LINE equals `8192)  # oracle: 8192 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: MAX_BODY_SIZE equals `10485760)  # oracle: 10485760 — named expected value from the requirement`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-LIB-COMMON-001
step("Read the shared limit constants")
expect(MAX_REQUEST_LINE).to_equal(8192)  # oracle: 8192 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(MAX_HEADER_COUNT).to_equal(100)  # oracle: 100 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(MAX_HEADER_LINE).to_equal(8192)  # oracle: 8192 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(MAX_BODY_SIZE).to_equal(10485760)  # oracle: 10485760 — named expected value from the requirement
```

